{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may not demand a security deposit larger than one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% annual interest once held a year, and return it within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 5% per year interest; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies of residential real property; the section states no building age, unit count or owner limits.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Interest is owed where the deposit is held for one year or longer; the 30-day return period runs from termination of the tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"Failure to deposit, itemize, transfer or return the deposit entitles the tenant to three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees; failure to hold it in a separate account gives immediate return.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts limit on upfront charges and fee in lieu of security deposit","requirement":"At or before a tenancy starts, a landlord or agent may require only first and last month's rent, a deposit equal to one month's rent, and key and lock costs; a fee in lieu of a deposit must be optional and total no more than one month's rent.","key_value":"first and last month's rent plus 1 month's rent deposit; fee in lieu total max 1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Any lessor or agent of a lessor of residential real property, at or prior to the commencement of a tenancy.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Charges are limited at or prior to the commencement of the tenancy; the fee-in-lieu option applies only where the lessor offers it.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"A tenant who agrees to a fee in lieu of a deposit may opt out by paying the full security deposit; fees paid plus the deposit may not exceed one month's rent.","penalty":"A lease provision conflicting with this section, or an attempt to obtain a waiver of it, forfeits the landlord's right to retain any portion of the security deposit.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy; and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu option must be offered without regard to income or credit score","requirement":"A landlord who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved applicant regardless of income, race, gender, disability, immigration status, household size or credit score, and may not use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit, for prospective tenants whose application for occupancy has been approved.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies where the lessor offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit and a prospective tenant's application for occupancy has been approved.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
